{"case_id":"T8084","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","state","input semantics"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["spng_decode_image","spng_decode_scanline","spng_decode_row"],"reason":"H0 can pass SPNG_DECODE_PROGRESSIVE through its fuzz-derived flags, but it always makes only one spng_decode_image() call and then frees ctx. In progressive mode, spng_decode_image() initializes decoding and returns 0; exercising the implicated continuation state requires subsequent spng_decode_scanline() or spng_decode_row() calls. H0 therefore misses the changed scanline error handling, including next-filter validation and decode_err() transitions. It also always supplies a non-NULL, exactly sized output buffer, so it does not cover the changed progressive/non-progressive out and len contract.","evidence":["H0 calls spng_decode_image(ctx, out, out_size, fmt, flags) exactly once and has no call to spng_decode_scanline() or spng_decode_row().","In S1, spng_decode_image() returns 0 immediately when flags & SPNG_DECODE_PROGRESSIVE after setting ctx->state = SPNG_STATE_DECODE_INIT.","The changed spng_decode_scanline() path now immediately routes read_scanline_bytes() failures through decode_err(ctx, ret) and defers an invalid next_filter to that same error path.","S1 moves the out == NULL and len < ctx->total_out_size checks under !(flags & SPNG_DECODE_PROGRESSIVE), while H0 always mallocs out_size bytes before calling spng_decode_image()."],"recommended_action":"Add a progressive-decoding harness path that calls spng_decode_image(ctx, NULL, 0, fmt, flags | SPNG_DECODE_PROGRESSIVE), then repeatedly invokes spng_decode_scanline() and/or spng_decode_row() with fuzz-controlled buffer lengths and call sequencing until completion or error; retain non-progressive cases with NULL and undersized output buffers."}
